From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Artur Szafraniec <ganggg111@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 20 Sep 2026 00:36:12 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] phy: samsung-ufs: Let a calibration table wait for the
 hardware to settle

A calibration sequence can need time to pass part way through a table,
between two writes that both belong to that table.  There is nowhere to
put that today: the PHY is powered on, and with it calibrated for the
first point, from inside the host's own link setup, so a settle time
that belongs between two of those writes cannot be moved out to either
side of the call.

Give a table an entry that only lets time pass.  It takes its turn like
any other entry, so the order stays the order the table is written in,
and it is not repeated per lane because time is not per lane.

Nothing uses it yet, so no SoC changes behaviour.

Signed-off-by: Artur Szafraniec <ganggg111@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/phy/samsung/phy-samsung-ufs.c | 10 ++++++++++
 drivers/phy/samsung/phy-samsung-ufs.h | 16 ++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 26 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/phy/samsung/phy-samsung-ufs.c b/drivers/phy/samsung/phy-samsung-ufs.c
index b5c0ba515fe..8ea818105d1 100644
--- a/drivers/phy/samsung/phy-samsung-ufs.c
+++ b/drivers/phy/samsung/phy-samsung-ufs.c
@@ -144,6 +144,11 @@ static int samsung_ufs_phy_calibrate(struct phy *phy)
 		if (!samsung_ufs_phy_cfg_applies(ufs_phy, cfg))
 			continue;
 
+		if (cfg->id == PHY_DELAY_BLK) {
+			udelay(cfg->val);
+			continue;
+		}
+
 		for_each_phy_lane(ufs_phy, i) {
 			samsung_ufs_phy_config(ufs_phy, cfg, i);
 		}
@@ -293,6 +298,11 @@ static int samsung_ufs_phy_notify_state(struct phy *phy,
 		if (!samsung_ufs_phy_cfg_applies(ufs_phy, cfg))
 			continue;
 
+		if (cfg->id == PHY_DELAY_BLK) {
+			udelay(cfg->val);
+			continue;
+		}
+
 		for_each_phy_lane(ufs_phy, i) {
 			samsung_ufs_phy_config(ufs_phy, cfg, i);
 		}
diff --git a/drivers/phy/samsung/phy-samsung-ufs.h b/drivers/phy/samsung/phy-samsung-ufs.h
index 94b28724000..77d2905b58f 100644
--- a/drivers/phy/samsung/phy-samsung-ufs.h
+++ b/drivers/phy/samsung/phy-samsung-ufs.h
@@ -15,6 +15,13 @@
 
 #define PHY_COMN_BLK	1
 #define PHY_TRSV_BLK	2
+/*
+ * An entry that only lets time pass.  A calibration sequence can need the
+ * hardware to settle part way through a table, between two writes that both
+ * belong to that table, which is a place no hook called around the table can
+ * reach.
+ */
+#define PHY_DELAY_BLK	3
 #define END_UFS_PHY_CFG { 0 }
 #define PHY_TRSV_CH_OFFSET	0x30
 #define PHY_APB_ADDR(off)	((off) << 2)
@@ -38,6 +45,15 @@
 #define PHY_TRSV_REG_CFG(o, v, d)	\
 	PHY_TRSV_REG_CFG_OFFSET(o, v, d, PHY_TRSV_CH_OFFSET)
 
+/* Let "u" microseconds pass before the rest of the table is written. */
+#define PHY_DELAY_CFG(u) {	\
+	.off_0 = 0,		\
+	.off_1 = 0,		\
+	.val = (u),		\
+	.desc = PWR_MODE_ANY,	\
+	.id = PHY_DELAY_BLK,	\
+}
+
 /* UFS PHY registers */
 #define PHY_PLL_LOCK_STATUS	0x1e
 
